# Config and Wire Data

Two kinds of data enter the game: **local config** (tuning values, tables, curves) and **wire data** (server payloads). They use different tools and must not be mixed up.

## Local config: ScriptableObjects, not runtime JSON

Game configuration lives in **ScriptableObject assets**, deserialized by Unity at load — not JSON or text files parsed at runtime.

- SO fields are Inspector-editable, diff-able, and cost zero parse time.
- Keep a reference to the SO and read fields live; do not copy SO fields into private primitives at init (Inspector edits during play would stop applying — see the no-config-access-wrappers rule).

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — parses a JSON at startup; not Inspector-editable
var cfg = JsonUtility.FromJson<TuningConfig>(File.ReadAllText(path));

// ✅ GOOD — SO asset, wired or loaded by address; fields read live
[SerializeField] private TuningConfig _config;
public float MoveSpeed => _config.moveSpeed;
```

## Wire data: explicit contracts, parsed once

- Wire DTOs live under a `Contracts/` folder and stay pure data (see the contracts-pure-dto rule).
- Declare explicit `[JsonProperty("field_name")]` on every serialized member; never rely on reflection-based name conventions (stripping hazard — see the no-reflection rule).
- Deserialize once per message, then convert to typed models at the ingestion boundary (see the parse-at-the-boundary rule). Never re-parse the same payload in multiple handlers.
- Parse and format numbers with `CultureInfo.InvariantCulture` (see the forbidden-apis rule).

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — two handlers each deserialize the same envelope
void OnBalance(string json) { var m = JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<Envelope>(json); ... }
void OnHistory(string json) { var m = JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<Envelope>(json); ... }

// ✅ GOOD — one deserialize, typed dispatch
void OnMessage(string json)
{
    var envelope = JsonConvert.DeserializeObject<Envelope>(json);
    Dispatch(envelope);
}
```

Runtime JSON parsing (`JsonUtility`, Newtonsoft) is reserved for wire data — never for local static config.

## Agent checklist

- [ ] Local config is a ScriptableObject asset, not runtime-parsed JSON/text
- [ ] SO configs read live via reference, not copied to primitives
- [ ] DTO members carry explicit `[JsonProperty]`
- [ ] Each payload deserialized once, converted at the boundary, never re-parsed downstream
